Sval: Notification.permission reads "default" where private windows are off

With dom.webnotifications.privateBrowsing.enabled false, which is Sval's
default, Notification.permission read "denied" on every site in a private
window and "default" in a normal one, so a page could tell a private window
from that one attribute. Where RFPTarget::PermissionsDefaultDenyPrompt hides
a global default's deny, the attribute reads "default" in a private window
too. A request is still refused, as a global default's is.

diff --git a/dom/notification/NotificationUtils.cpp b/dom/notification/NotificationUtils.cpp
